      "standards": null,
      "comments": []
    },
    {
      "id": "msg-2",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "I designed a desk phone stand in molded ABS that holds the phone at 70°. It passes all 3 checks that apply: material, minimum wall of 2 mm and minimum draft of 1°. The check report lists no risks.\n\n- **Base:** a plate 95 × 80 mm, 3 mm thick.\n- **Front:** a lip 12 mm tall, with a 14 mm slot behind it where the bottom edge of the phone sits.\n- **Back rest:** 100 mm long, set at 70° from the desk.\n- **Rear strut:** runs the full width and braces the back rest.\n- **Draft:** the first version failed the draft check at the front lip (0° against the 1° minimum). I fixed it by tapering the outside and the lip by 1.5°.\n\n**Assumptions:**\n- **Slot width:** 14 mm, so it fits a phone in a case.\n- **Mould direction:** I assumed the part comes out of the mould straight up.\n\nStrength, how steady it is on a desk, drop and heat aren't checked, so please review them by hand. Next I could add a slot for a charging cable through the lip and base, or you can change the width or slot width in the parameters.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-18T10:42:23.868589Z",
      "model": null,
      "effort": null,
